00:26:34.010 --> 00:26:37.250
And, again, just another note
to wrap this session before we

00:26:37.250 --> 00:26:40.580
open to questions-- and very
much encouraging questions--

00:26:40.580 --> 00:26:42.787
is that what is key across
all these initiatives

00:26:42.787 --> 00:26:44.370
and what we've
discussed today, again,

00:26:44.370 --> 00:26:48.920
is this idea of cooperation--
of looking across industries

00:26:48.920 --> 00:26:51.050
and really looking
at what can everyone

00:26:51.050 --> 00:26:53.240
bring to the table
in these initiatives.

00:26:53.240 --> 00:26:56.120
There are experts across a
variety of different areas--

00:26:56.120 --> 00:27:00.560
whether that's biodiversity
or food systems or even

00:27:00.560 --> 00:27:02.870
students working around
data visualization and data

00:27:02.870 --> 00:27:06.290
analysis-- and working together
and making these opportunities

00:27:06.290 --> 00:27:09.740
available, we can accomplish
some pretty exciting things

00:27:09.740 --> 00:27:12.590
and work towards addressing
some of the world's greatest

00:27:12.590 --> 00:27:13.490
challenges.

00:27:13.490 --> 00:27:17.440
[MUSIC PLAYING]

